    "explanation": "This is a driver-terminated no-show cancellation on TRP-02745, and the verified no-show fee stands. To the rider: your own device data does not support 'I never saw the car'. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02745) puts your phone 784 to 790 metres from the pickup pin for the whole waiting window, with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, while the driver's own trace holds him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius continuously from 18:06:05 to 18:12:45 - one unbroken 400-second run of 41 consecutive in-geofence fixes. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold: (a) the trip record (EV-TRIP-02745) carries a driver 'arrived' event at 18:06:05; (b) the first qualifying in-geofence fix is at that same timestamp, with a dwell start offset of 0.0 s; (c) the 400-second dwell measured from the first in-geofence fix exceeds the 180-second free waiting period in force (platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180); and (d) the trip was terminated by the driver at 18:12:48 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW - one of the three codes limb (d) recognises - with no boarding event and no started_at. To the driver: the arrival marker is genuine, not a false-arrival event. At the marker timestamp you were at the pin (minimum recorded distance 0.16 m), so POL-NS-05's triggers (over 300 m from the pin, or 15 km/h or more at the marker) are not engaged, and no POL-NS-05 referral arises. POL-NS-06 does not rescue the rider either: your dwell is a single unbroken 400-second run, so the accumulation route in limb (i) is not needed - and it would have been unavailable in any event, because the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02745-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and POL-NS-06(i) requires a present, populated advisory. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: limb (a) requires a locating or coordinating message from the rider during the waiting window, and the only message in EV-CHAT-02745 was sent by you ('im at the pickup point', 18:06:25, read 18:06:55); the rider replied to nothing and placed no in-app call. POL-NS-03 and POL-NS-10 have no application - the driver's stationary fixes were inside the radius, and the cancellation was the driver's, not the rider's. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-02745) shows a single cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued 0.00, reconciling exactly with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of 4.50, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect and no basis to disturb the amount charged. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force - SGD 3.60, the net figure and never the rider's gross SGD 6.61 - the residual 20 percent being the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 132 is 0.0076, below the 0.08 rate limb; both limbs must hold and neither does. The rider's prior_no_show_flags and prior_disputes_filed are lifetime counters and context only under POL-GEN-01; they were mentioned only to say they cannot ground a finding, and no adverse finding rests on them. The charge to the rider is left as it stands, which POL-NS-07 describes as NO_ACTION on the fee; the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION because that is the outcome the case produces, and per POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 as driver_compensation_sgd - this is the amount the ruling moves, not a second payment and not a refund to the rider. No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 fires: the instrument artifacts agree rather than contradict on arrival and dwell, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, and the deciding facts rest on COMPLETE, weight-1.0 artifacts. My confidence cap is 1.0 - the minimum weight of EV-GPS-02745 and EV-TRIP-02745, which carry the deciding facts, both COMPLETE at weight 1.0 - so the cap does not bite, and I record 0.95. The monetary effect of SGD 3.60 is below the