    "explanation": "To both parties: the rider's dispute is not upheld, and the driver is paid his share of the fee.\n\nARRIVAL AND DWELL (both advocates, and the deciding facts). The trip was terminated by the driver at 18:12:48 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes POL-NS-01 limb (d) recognises, with no boarding event and no started_at on the record (EV-TRIP-02745). The driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 18:06:05, and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02745) places his first qualifying in-geofence fix at that same second — dwell-start offset 0.0 s — and keeps him inside the STANDARD 50 m arrival radius continuously from 18:06:05 to 18:12:45: 400 seconds of dwell across 41 qualifying fixes, against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is not set). His minimum recorded distance to the pin is 0.16 m. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold, and the cancellation at 18:12:48 fell about 3 minutes 43 seconds after the required dwell elapsed at 18:09:05.\n\nCLAUSES THAT COULD DISPLACE THE FEE. POL-NS-05: the arrival marker was not false — the driver was 0.16 m from the pin and stationary at the marker, well inside the 300 m and 15 km/h triggers, so the waiting clock was not recomputed. POL-NS-06: there is no dwell shortfall (400 s against 180 s), so the fee is chargeable whether or not the rider was present. POL-NS-03: it does not apply, because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue. POL-NS-04: the rider cannot be exonerated, because limb (a) fails — the chat log (EV-CHAT-02745) holds exactly one message, sent by the driver at 18:06:25 ('im at the pickup point'), delivered 18:06:26 and read at 18:06:55, and the rider sent no locating or coordinating message and placed no in-app call. POL-NS-10: inapplicable, because the rider did not cancel this trip.\n\nTHE RIDER'S ACCOUNT. The claim 'I never saw the car' is not supported. The rider's own device track puts her 784.4 m to 790.5 m from the pickup pin, stationary, for the whole window, with zero fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius (EV-GPS-02745, rider_track). That does not help her either way: the fee does not depend on her presence, and with no message from her POL-NS-04 cannot apply.\n\nINTEGRITY AND ESCALATION. The POL-NS-08 checks are clean: the arrived timestamp matches a GPS fix to the second (no clock skew); the trace has no sampling gaps, 79 fixes at 10-second cadence and a rider track present; the chat log's single message matches trip_record.chat_message_count of 1; and the fare line of SGD 4.50 equals the net cancellation fee in force, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: the trip record and the trace agree rather than contradict on arrival and dwell, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, and the deciding facts rest on COMPLETE weight-1.0 artifacts. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02745-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact this ruling rests on and does not lower confidence.\n\nMONEY. POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee in force = SGD 3.60, the residual SGD 0.90 (20 percent) being retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 / completed_trips_30d of 132 = 0.0076, below the 0.08 rate — both limbs must hold and neither does, so compensation is not withheld (the driver's concession on this point and on the 6.7-minute wait timer does not defeat the fee, which is measured by GPS). The ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and, per POL-GEN-03, amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60; the rider's SGD 4.50 charge stands as it presently is (NO_ACTION as to the fee). The rider's prior_no_show_flags and prior_disputes_filed are lifetime counters and context only under POL-GEN-01; they were not used as a ground against her. The monetary effect of SGD 3.60 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes automatically. No clause produces a referral."
